        "content": "<p>I am trying to prove the following:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">\\</span><span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">\\</span><span class=\"n\">le</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">6</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">\\</span><span class=\"n\">le</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>and just totally stuck. Are there any hints I could ask the community for? it seems obvious and yet?</p>",
        "id": 631799501,
        "sender_full_name": "Fred Grim",
        "timestamp": 1792020227
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Hey, for formatting see <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib/wiki/Code-in-backticks\">#backticks</a> and <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mwe.html\">#mwe</a><br>\nWhat kind of hints are you looking for? There are tactics that'll solve it immediately, and ones which will need a bit more work.</p>",
        "id": 631799729,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1792020340
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>the ones that need more work. I want to figure out why I find this so challenging. Thank you so much</p>",
        "id": 631800198,
        "sender_full_name": "Fred Grim",
        "timestamp": 1792020546
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Then logically I'd proceed by case splitting on <code>k = 0 ∨ 0 &lt; k</code>, then <code>k = 1 ∨ 1 &lt; k</code>, then <code>k = 2 ∨ 2 &lt; k</code>.<br>\nThe key lemma here is <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Nat.eq_or_lt_of_le#doc\">docs#Nat.eq_or_lt_of_le</a>, with either <code>cases</code> or <code>rcases</code>, and to go to the next case split you can use <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Nat.add_one_le_of_lt#doc\">docs#Nat.add_one_le_of_lt</a>.</p>",
        "id": 631800722,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1792020835
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Actually maybe <code>by_contra!</code> could go right to the end, where you have to reason about squaring being monotonic anyways</p>",
        "id": 631800820,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1792020884
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>You can also argue that it suffices to prove that <code>k &lt; 3</code>, then that it suffices <code>k ^ 2 &lt; 9</code> and then conclude.</p>",
        "id": 631800949,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1792020950
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ok I think I can work with that. I wanted to avoid contradiction only because I am going through exercises in a book and the author hasn’t gotten to contradiction yet. So it would feel like cheating. Thanks so much for the hints</p>",
        "id": 631805030,
        "sender_full_name": "Fred Grim",
        "timestamp": 1792022768
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>One line:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">6</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">nlinarith</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
